I'm putting the items into the lesson in alphabetical order. The lesson wil=
l
be in alphabetical order. The purpose of the lesson is to learn the gismu,
including the various places. It is not intended to be used in conjunction
with any other learning materials.

It is possible- and rather easy, to put the same item into multiple lessons=
.
It would not be difficult to, for instance, make a "Lojban for Beginners"
lesson, and add the items in the "Lojban gismu" lesson to it in the order
they appear in the "Lojban for Beginners" lessons.

The teaching programs in Smart.fm do not necessarily go in alphabetical
order. The iKnow! program *starts* in the order that the items are entered
in, but as you progress, the items that you remember better appear less
often, while those you are having trouble with appear more often, without
regard to the original order they appear in. Drill Beta seems to be about
the same as iKnow!, with minor differences. BrainSpeed, which is a review
program, never bothers with the order of the items, but merely chooses them
at random.

